const enBody = `
<h1 id="top">Scaleway Generative APIs Review 2026: EU Per-Token Pricing and the Paris-Only Residency Rule</h1>

<p>Scaleway is a French cloud provider that started as a bare-metal and GPU-hosting company and grew into a full European hyperscaler with GPU Instances, Object Storage, Containers, and a managed inference product called <strong>Generative APIs</strong>. For an API catalog, Scaleway is interesting for one reason above all others: it is the rare provider that publishes a clean, self-hosted, per-million-token price card in euros for models you can actually call, hosted inside the European Union, with no marketplace markup and no reseller chain in between.</p>

<p>That combination puts Scaleway into a narrow band. It is not the cheapest provider in the market — Groq, Cerebras, DeepInfra, and Fireworks all undercut several of these rates in USD. It is not the widest catalog either — OpenRouter carries 457 models against Scaleway's 17 serverless entries. What Scaleway is, and what almost nothing else is, is <strong>a first-party European cloud selling European-hosted inference at published EUR rates</strong>, with an SLA attached, a free tier, and a batch discount. If your procurement checklist contains a data-residency line item, that is the reason to read the rest of this review.</p>

<p>We verified every price below against the live Scaleway Model-as-a-Service pricing page and the Generative APIs documentation on <strong>October 29, 2026</strong>. The table has changed since our last crawl 42 days ago: the lineup now includes GLM-5.3 and GLM-5.2, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, Qwen 3.8 27B, and Gemma 4 26B A4B, while Qwen 3 235B Thinking 2507 has dropped off the serverless list. Prices are quoted before tax, in euros, and are not normalized to any other currency.</p>

<h2 id="two-modes">Two deployment modes, two billing models</h2>

<p>Scaleway splits its inference product into two distinct offerings, and confusing them is the most common mistake when reading the pricing page.</p>

<p><strong>Serverless</strong> is the pay-per-token product. You call a pre-configured endpoint, you pay for tokens consumed, and you never touch a GPU. Billing starts at token 1,000,001 because the first million are free. This is what most developers should start with, and it is where the per-model prices below apply.</p>

<p><strong>Dedicated Deployment</strong> is a managed GPU instance running a model you select. You pick a GPU instance type from the Scaleway hardware range, Scaleway provisions it, you deploy an optimized model onto it, and you are billed per GPU hour for the time the deployment exists. Critically, billing only starts once the model is actually deployed — not while you are waiting for it. The rates run from EUR 0.93/hour for an L4 up to EUR 30.06/hour for an 8-way H100 SXM cluster.</p>

<p>The practical read: Serverless is for spiky, unpredictable, or pre-launch traffic. Dedicated Deployment is for steady high-volume workloads where you want predictable throughput, no rate limits, and a hardware choice. A production system often ends up using both — serverless for the long tail of small models and dedicated for the one model that carries your main volume.</p>

<h2 id="serverless-pricing">Serverless pricing: the full 17-model table</h2>

<p>This is the complete serverless catalog as published, with input and output rates per million tokens. Cached-input rates are listed where Scaleway publishes them separately.</p>

<table>
<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Tasks</th><th>Input</th><th>Cached input</th><th>Output</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>qwen3-embedding-8b</td><td>Embeddings</td><td>EUR 0.10/M</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>bge-multilingual-gemma2</td><td>Embeddings</td><td>EUR 0.10/M</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct-2506</td><td>Chat and Vision</td><td>EUR 0.15/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 0.35/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>gpt-oss-120b</td><td>Chat</td><td>EUR 0.15/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 0.60/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>gemma-4-26b-a4b-it</td><td>Chat, code, and Vision</td><td>EUR 0.25/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 0.50/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>qwen3.6-35b-a3b</td><td>Chat, code, and Vision</td><td>EUR 0.25/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 1.50/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>deepseek-v4-flash-0731</td><td>Chat and code</td><td>EUR 0.40/M</td><td>EUR 0.08/M</td><td>EUR 0.80/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>deepseek-v4.1-flash</td><td>Chat, code, and Vision</td><td>EUR 0.60/M</td><td>EUR 0.12/M</td><td>EUR 1.80/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>qwen3.5-397b-a17b</td><td>Chat, code, and Vision</td><td>EUR 0.60/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 3.60/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>qwen3.8-27b</td><td>Chat, code, and Vision</td><td>EUR 0.60/M</td><td>EUR 0.12/M</td><td>EUR 3.30/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507</td><td>Chat</td><td>EUR 0.75/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 2.25/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>llama-3.3-70b-instruct</td><td>Chat</td><td>EUR 0.90/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 0.90/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>mistral-medium-3.5-128b</td><td>Chat, code, and Vision</td><td>EUR 1.50/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 7.50/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>glm-5.3</td><td>Chat and code</td><td>EUR 1.80/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 5.50/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>glm-5.2</td><td>Chat and code</td><td>EUR 1.80/M</td><td>—</td><td>EUR 5.50/M</td></tr>
<tr><td>lightonocr-3-0.8b</td><td>OCR</td><td>EUR 2.20/M</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
<tr><td>whisper-large-v3</td><td>Audio transcription</td><td>EUR 0.003/audio min</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
